[00:00.00]If you want to become excellent at anything, you do not need a perfect life, a special talent,|如果你想在任何领域变得出色，你不需要完美的人生、特殊的天赋，
[00:05.08]or one big heroic moment. You need three simple things, clear goals, steady consistency,|也不需要某个英雄时刻。你只需要三件简单的事：清晰的目标、稳定的坚持，
[00:11.38]and real patience. These three ideas work together. Goals give you direction. Consistency|和真正的耐心。这三者相互配合：目标给你方向，坚持
[00:18.62]keeps you moving. Patience helps you stay on the path long enough to see results.|让你持续前进，耐心让你在这条路上待得足够久，直到看见结果。
[00:23.78]First, you need a goal.|第一，你需要一个目标。
[00:25.84]A goal is like the top of a mountain.|目标就像山顶。
[00:28.68]Without a peak, there is no mountain to climb.|没有山峰，就没有山可爬。
[00:31.96]But here is the mistake many people make.|但很多人会犯这样一个错误：
[00:34.36]They choose a big goal, then they spend all their time thinking about it, talking about it, and dreaming about it.|他们选了一个大目标，然后把所有时间都用来想它、说它、梦它。
[00:40.64]That can feel exciting, but it is not the same as doing the work.|那确实让人兴奋，但这跟真正去做是两回事。
[00:44.90]A big goal can also feel scary.|大目标也会让人害怕。
[00:48.16]If you only look at the top of the mountain, you may feel too far away and want to quit.|如果你只盯着山顶，会觉得太远，就想放弃。
[00:53.02]A better way is to choose your big goal, break it into smaller parts, and then focus on what|更好的做法是：选定大目标，把它拆成小块，然后专注在
[00:58.52]you can do today.|今天能做的事上。
[01:00.26]If your goal is to get stronger, do not think every day about the final number you want|如果你的目标是变强壮，别每天想着最终要举起的
[01:05.12]to lift.|那个重量，
[01:06.42]Think about today's workout.|想想今天的训练。
[01:08.42]If your goal is to learn English, do not worry every day about speaking perfectly.|如果你的目标是学英语，别每天担心说得完不完美，
[01:13.46]Focus on learning 10 new words, reading one short article, or practicing for 15 minutes.|而是专注学 10 个新词、读一篇短文，或者练 15 分钟。
[01:20.10]steps make big goals possible. This is called focusing on the process, not only the result.|小步让大目标成为可能。这就叫专注过程，而不只是结果。
[01:26.78]The result matters of course. Winning feels good. Achieving a dream feels good. But if you believe,|结果当然重要，赢的感觉很好，实现梦想的感觉很好。但如果你认定
[01:34.26]when I finally reach this goal, then I will be happy, you may fall into a trap.|「等我达成目标，我就会幸福」，就可能掉进陷阱。
[01:39.52]Many people work for years to reach something, feel happy for a short time, and then feel empty|很多人努力多年达成某件事，短暂开心之后，又觉得空虚。
[01:45.10]again. Why? Because lasting satisfaction usually does not come only from the final moment.|为什么？因为持久的满足感通常不只来自最后那一刻，
[01:51.98]It comes from the daily work, the growth, the effort, and the person you become along the way.|而来自每天的努力、成长、付出，以及一路上你成为的那个人。
[01:58.40]A useful way to set goals is to make them specific and clear. For example,|一个实用的定目标方法，是让目标具体、清晰。比如，
[02:03.86]I want to improve my English is too general. A stronger goal is, I want to have a 5-minute|「我想提高英语」太笼统。更有力的目标是「我想在三个月内
[02:10.40]English conversation in three months. This goal is specific, easy to measure, connected to action,|用英语聊 5 分钟」。这个目标具体、可衡量、和行动挂钩、
[02:17.90]meaningful, and has a deadline. Once you have that goal, you can create a simple plan.|有意义，而且有期限。有了目标，就可以做一个简单的计划：
[02:24.18]Practice speaking 10 minutes a day, learn useful sentences, listen to beginner English videos,|每天练说 10 分钟，学实用句子，听初级英语视频，
[02:30.20]and review every week. The second key is consistency. Today, social media often shows|每周复盘。第二个关键是坚持。如今社交媒体常常展示
[02:37.34]extreme effort, people working all night, training until they cannot stand or pushing themselves like|极端的努力：通宵工作、练到站不起来，或者像超级英雄一样逼自己。
[02:43.32]superheroes. This looks impressive, but excellence is usually not built by one heroic day. It is|看起来很厉害，但出色通常不是靠某一天的英雄壮举，
[02:50.46]built by many good days repeated for months and years. You do not need to destroy yourself.|而是靠很多个好日子，重复数月数年。你不需要把自己毁掉，
[02:56.44]You need to show up again and again. Think of progress like exercise. If you train so hard|你需要一次又一次地出现。把进步想成锻炼：如果你今天练得太狠，
[03:02.20]today that you cannot move for a week, that is not smart. It is better to train in a way that|一周都动不了，那不明智。更好的方式是，用
[03:07.38]allows you to come back tomorrow. Most of your efforts should feel challenging but manageable,|让你明天还能回来的强度去练。大多数时候的努力，应该是有挑战但扛得住，
[03:13.44]maybe a 6 or 7 out of 10. If every day is a 10 out of 10 you will burn out. If every day is too|大概 10 分里 6 到 7 分。如果每天都拼到 10 分，你会耗竭；如果每天都太
[03:19.88]easy, you will not grow. The goal is to find a rhythm you can repeat. There is a popular idea|轻松，你就不会成长。目标是找到一个你能重复的节奏。有个流行的说法
[03:26.22]that says, get 1% better every day. As a mindset, it is powerful. It reminds us that small improvements|叫「每天进步 1%」。作为一种心态，它很有力量，提醒我们小进步
[03:34.74]matter. But in real life, progress does not happen in a straight line. At the beginning,|很重要。但现实中，进步不是一条直线。一开始，
[03:40.56]you may improve very fast. Then progress becomes slower. Later, you may reach a plateau where it|你可能进步飞快，然后慢下来，再后来会遇到平台期，
[03:47.24]feels like nothing is changing. This is normal. It does not mean you are failing. It means you|感觉什么都没变。这很正常，不代表你在失败，而代表你
[03:53.50]have entered a deeper stage of learning. When you hit a plateau, you need more than motivation.|进入了更深的学习阶段。遇到平台期时，你需要的不仅是动力，
[03:59.22]You need curiosity, discipline, and commitment. You need to ask, what can I learn here? Maybe|还需要好奇心、自律和投入。你要问自己：我能在这里学到什么？也许
[04:06.22]your method needs a small change. Maybe you need more rest. Maybe you simply need more time.|方法需要微调，也许你需要更多休息，也许你只是需要更多时间。
[04:13.48]Even when you cannot see progress, experience is still building under the surface.|即使看不到进步，经验也在水面之下不断积累。
[04:18.80]That leads to the third key, patience.|这就引出了第三个关键：耐心。
[04:21.80]There is no true overnight success.|真正的「一夜成名」并不存在。
[04:24.40]Great achievements in sports, art, business, study, or any skill usually take years.|体育、艺术、商业、学业或任何技能上的伟大成就，通常都需要多年。
[04:31.14]The modern world makes us want everything fast.|现代世界让我们什么都想快。
[04:34.18]Messages are fast.|消息要快，
[04:36.02]Videos are fast.|视频要快，
[04:37.86]News is fast.|新闻要快。
[04:39.46]But meaningful growth is often slow.|但真正有意义的成长往往是慢的。
[04:42.22]You cannot rush it.|你催不来。
[04:43.18]If you rush too much, you may get injured, tired, stressed, or disappointed.|太急，你可能会受伤、疲惫、焦虑或失望。
[04:49.76]Patience means understanding that plateaus are part of the journey.|耐心，就是明白平台期是旅程的一部分。
[04:54.26]Imagine hitting a stone with a hammer.|想象你用锤子敲一块石头。
[04:56.56]The stone may break on the 30-second hit, but the first 31 hits still matter.|石头可能在第三十下时裂开，但前 31 下同样重要——
[05:01.32]They are building pressure inside the stone.|它们在石头内部积蓄压力。
[05:03.82]Your work is the same.|你的努力也是一样。
[05:05.76]Every practice session, every small effort, every quiet day of showing up is building something.|每一次练习、每一分小小的努力、每一个默默坚持的日子，都在积累些什么，
[05:11.96]even if you cannot see it yet. This is why small daily objectives are so important.|哪怕你还看不见。这就是为什么每天的小目标如此重要。
[05:18.30]If you are climbing a mountain, staring at the peak all day can make you feel hopeless.|爬山时，如果整天盯着山顶，你会觉得绝望，
[05:23.60]You may also trip because you are not watching your next step. But if your goal today is just|还可能因为没看脚下而绊倒。但如果今天的目标只是
[05:29.20]to climb the next small section, you can stay focused. Big goals need small victories.|爬完下一小段，你就能保持专注。大目标需要小胜利。
[05:35.30]These small victories give you energy and keep you moving. So choose a meaningful goal.|这些小胜利给你能量，让你继续走。所以，选一个有意义的目标，
[05:41.86]Break it down into small actions.|把它拆成小行动，
[05:44.22]Focus on today's step.|专注今天的这一步，
[05:46.56]Show up consistently, but do not burn yourself out.|稳定地出现，但别把自己耗干，
[05:50.16]Expect slow seasons and plateaus.|接受缓慢的时期和平台期，
[05:52.90]Be patient enough to keep going.|耐心到足以继续走下去。
[05:55.36]Excellence is not one big moment.|出色不是某一个伟大的瞬间，
[05:58.02]It is a way of living, practicing, learning, and returning to the path every time you fall off.|而是一种生活方式：练习、学习，每次跌倒后都回到路上。
[06:03.96]The peak matters, but the real growth happens during the climb.|山顶很重要，但真正的成长发生在攀登的过程中。
